Z||000009||chester||09-08-2001||07:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by billfredmike24:<BR><B>Can you paint the pan?(bottom peice that covers up the hole) to match the rest of your car?  And when you lift the hood up do the lights come up with it like this guys do, or is that his own mod?<P>[This message has been edited by billfredmike24 (edited 09-08-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I guess you could.  They come flat black and I don't know what effect painting them a (I'm assuming) gloss color would have.  Expecially with glare.  If your refering the to black GT that belongs to me and the lights come the way you see them.  They mount to the hood with the two bolts that hold the light covers on.  Hope this helps.<P>Rob D.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front1_1.JPG"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
